 6/08/FF-September-JM.jpg
UID:8OEXa6gozHu54HhbZx1Vw
SUMMARY:First Fridays Presents John Milkereit
DTSTAMP:20260818T032835Z
DTSTART:20260904T193000Z
DESCRIPTION:Free and open to the public \nDoors @ 7 pm\nReading @ 7:30 pm\n
	Followed by an Open mic \nInprint is proud to serve as the host for the Fi
	rst Fridays Reading Series. The First Fridays Reading Series is the oldest
	 poetry series in Houston and was organized by Robert Clark from 1975-2019
	. Today\, First Fridays events are curated and hosted by local community m
	embers. \nThe September featured reader will be John Milkereit. John lives
	 in Houston\, Texas working as a mechanical engineer. His poetry journey d
	id not begin well after being forced to read “Beowulf” in 6th grade. Sever
	al decades later\, he found himself enjoying a poetry seminar at his local
	 church on the poetry of Billy Collins\, and then he took his first poetry
	 class at Inprint in 2005. Later\, he went on to complete an MFA in Creati
	ve Writing at the Rainier Writing Workshop. His poems have since appeared 
	in various literary journals such as The Comstock Review\, San Pedro River
	 Review\, and Naugatuck River Review. In December\, Kelsay Books released 
	his fifth collection of poems entitled\, The Beginning of Undoing. \nFor m
	ore information about the First Fridays Reading Series\, click here. To jo
	in the First Fridays Facebook group\, click here. \n\n\nhttps://inprinthou
	ston.org/event/first-fridays-presents-john-milkereit/\n\nFrom Inprint Hous
	ton
URL:https://inprinthouston.org/event/first-fridays-presents-john-milkereit/
LOCATION:Inprint House\, 1520 W Main St\, Houston\, TX\, 77006\, United Sta
	tes
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:inprint-houston
CATEGORIES:Inprint Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
