IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://inprinthouston.org
 /wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Whitehead_Colson_Headshot-Credit_Chris-Close-f
 or-website.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://inprinthouston.org/wp-content/uploads/202
 6/07/Whitehead_Colson_Headshot-Credit_Chris-Close-for-website.jpg
UID:hfbct1_AA8Dzf7muYJOkR
SUMMARY:Inprint Colson Whitehead Reading
DTSTAMP:20260818T032835Z
DTSTART:20261112T193000Z
DESCRIPTION:General admission tickets for $35\, which will include a copy o
	f Colson Whitehead’s Cool Machine\, and will go on sale on Tuesday\, Octob
	er 13\, 2026 at 12 pm. Season tickets are on sale here. \nColson Whitehead
	 will read from his new novel Cool Machine\, followed by an on-stage conve
	rsation with a local author/journalist. The evening will conclude with a b
	ook sale and signing. The event is presented as part of the 2026/2027 Inpr
	int Margarett Root Brown Reading Series.  \nTwo-time Pulitzer Prize and Na
	tional Book Award winner and #1 New York Times bestselling author Colson W
	hitehead comes to Houston with his new novel Cool Machine\, the magnificen
	t and highly anticipated final volume of his Harlem Trilogy that brings to
	 life 1980s New York. In a starred review\, Publishers Weekly writes\, “Wh
	itehead concludes his Harlem Trilogy with a transcendent and wildly entert
	aining novel in which his recurring characters grapple with the ways their
	 lives are defined by crime and the city they call home. . . . The heists\
	, stakeouts\, and showdowns are rendered with grit and precision\, but the
	 real wallops come in breathtaking riffs on the city’s magnetic force. . .
	 . It’s the greatest New York novel in years.” \nWhitehead is the first wr
	iter to win the Pulitzer for consecutive books: the historical novels The 
	Underground Railroad (2016) and The Nickel Boys (2019). The Underground Ra
	ilroad also won the National Book Award and was named one of the Ten Best 
	Books of the Year by The New York Times Book Review. Known for innovative 
	novels that explore social themes\, while often incorporating fantastical 
	elements\, he is also the author of The Intuitionist\, John Henry Days\, a
	nd Sag Harbor\, as well as The Colossus of New York\, a book of essays abo
	ut the city\, and The Noble Hustle\, a nonfiction account about the 2011 W
	orld Series of Poker. Among his honors\, Whitehead has received MacArthur 
	and Guggenheim Fellowships\, a Whiting Writers Award\, the Library of Cong
	ress Prize for American Fiction\, and the National Humanities Medal. From 
	2018-2020\, he served as the New York State Author. \n\n\nhttps://inprinth
	ouston.org/event/inprint-colson-whitehead-reading-2/\n\nFrom Inprint Houst
	on
URL:https://inprinthouston.org/event/inprint-colson-whitehead-reading-2/
LOCATION:Congregation Emanu El\, 1500 Sunset Boulevard\, Houston\, TX\, 770
	05
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:inprint-houston
CATEGORIES:Inprint Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
